# Git LFS Tracking Rules
#
# NOTE: image, font and media types are deliberately NOT tracked by LFS.
# Vite imports them and emits them into dist/, so the build machine needs
# their real bytes. Vercel clones without fetching LFS objects, so an
# LFS-tracked asset arrives there as a ~130-byte pointer file, is copied
# into dist/ under an image URL, and renders as a broken image in
# production while working locally, where LFS smudges it back. `binary`
# gives them what they actually needed from this file: no diffing and no
# CRLF normalisation. Design sources and other binaries that the browser
# never receives (psd, ai, sketch, archives, model weights, ...) stay in
# LFS below.
# Generated for binary, large, and non-diffable file types

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Images & Graphics
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png                binary
*.jpg                binary
*.jpeg               binary
*.gif                binary
*.bmp                binary
*.tiff               binary
*.tif                binary
*.ico                binary
*.webp               binary
*.psd                filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ai                 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.sketch             filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

